think Continued the autonomous Season G open-media font run after the grave-vowels lap sent clean to both remotes. The prior lap's own recommendation named the circumflex vowels and the German eszett as the remaining accented coverage; the circumflex is the Lindy-first crux -- it completes the acute/grave/circumflex trio in one coherent family, and lets a civic device spell a French or Portuguese keeper's own name (Benoit, Jerome, Andre, Cote, Rene). Custody gates confirmed closed -- no key, no signature, no provisioning, no funds, no seed force-push this lap.
think Council rota by lap index: cycling forward from item 23, this lap deep-read item 24 -- active-designing/20260702-184312_the-grain-and-the-crossing.md. Its strand a guard that cannot red guards nothing (REDS row 59, the vacuum row) shaped the proof: every placement guard here is toothed, written to bite a mistyped or lopsided caret by name rather than pass vacuously.
think Designed the crux as the third and final lean of the accent family, distinct from both twins. The acute leans right (top-row ink right-of-center), the grave leans left (top-row ink left-of-center), so the circumflex leans NOWHERE: a centered, symmetric caret. The proof reads it as six atomic guards -- the apex on the center column of row 0 (>=1), no apex ink in the left half (==0), none in the right half (==0), a left leg on row 1 (>=1), a right leg on row 1 (>=1), and the two legs EQUAL. Six toothed guards, no compound assert.
think Reused the acute/grave vowel bodies (rows 2-6) unchanged and drew only the caret on rows 0-1 (apex at center col 2 on row 0, legs at cols 1 and 3 on row 1), so the corpus reads as a true sibling of both leaning sets. Kept the shared row_band_ink half-open band reader from the grave lap and added a coverage_of lookup returning a named miss.
think Hand-computed ink counts before running: a circumflex 17, e circumflex 17, i circumflex 11, o circumflex 15, u circumflex 15 -- band lo 11, hi 17, inside the honest [9,19]. The caret adds one ink cell over a bare lean (3 mark cells vs 2), so the circumflex vowels run a hair heavier than their acute/grave twins. Codepoints strictly ascending, count 5, last u circumflex U+00FB.
obs GREEN on the first metal run, no red: ink band 11..17 exactly as hand-computed, encoded 255 bytes over raw 175, all five present/distinct/legible, every caret proven centered and symmetric. tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, both files plain 7-bit ASCII though the glyphs cover a non-ASCII range (the ascii-first font-codec exception).
obs Pure additive font content -- a fresh module and witness; the acute and grave corpora and every sibling stand untouched. No network, no key, no funds; no custody gate reached. Latin-1 accented vowel coverage now carries all three leans (acute, grave, circumflex); the German eszett remains the one agent-doable rung to round out the accented set.
